  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "<em>uk1 kei2</em> (屋企) is the natural Cantonese for 'home' — much more colloquial than the formal 家. To talk about going home, <strong>faan1 uk1 kei2</strong> (返屋企, literally 'return home'). Room names are distinct compounds rather than English-style: <em>cyu4 fong2</em> (廚房, kitchen), <em>ci3 so2</em> (廁所, toilet), <em>haak3 teng1</em> (客廳, living room). For 'bedroom', most people just say <em>fong2</em> (房) — the formal <em>fong4 gaan1</em> (房間) sits in writing or service contexts.",
